  "chance_is_structural": "twin members are byte-identical with opposite correct labels. A prompt-only strategy must answer both members the same way, so it scores exactly 0.500 per row and exactly 0.000 on pairs; a row-independent coin flip scores 0.250 on pairs. The 0.500 pair threshold in the gate below is therefore well above the null and is conservative, not the null itself.",
